extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading and lore start on printed 82, the abilities and skill lists fill printed 83, and the equipment, money and cybernetics end at the top of printed 84, where the Fly Boy begins. GROUP: listed in the book''s Coalition Military O.C.C.s section (printed 67) and described as trained soldiers as well as scientists, so men-of-arms and men_of_arms true, as the Coalition Technical Officer is. MONEY: 1D4x1000 credits to start, which the book prints outright; the monthly salary is 1,900 credits plus combat pay, with room, board and clothing free. The text layer reads the dice as a cipher; confirmed 1D4x1000 and 1900 from a render. MOS: the four +15% skills from one area are modelled as skills.mos, one option per area, each a choice of four; the +15% is taken as the MOS figure in place of the ordinary category bonus. SAVES: the horror factor and magic save steps are level-gated and stored in at_level; the possession save applies from level one; save vs magic is stored as spell_magic. The geomancy lore is kept as a special ability with its own 30% +5% rather than granted as the catalog''s Lore: Geomancy or Lines of Power row, which is tagged Nightbane only. Starting equipment names fine leather gloves (stored as the plain gloves row), 2D4 specimen containers (specimen-jar), two satchels (purse-satchel), a utility/combat harness (battle-harness), a laser scalpel equivalent to Wilk''s (wilk-s-laser-scalpel), the PC-3000 hand-held computer (portable-hand-held-computer) and a PDD pocket audio recorder; plastic bags have no row. Dress uniform is listed twice in the book and stored once."
